<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#akuapem-twi">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akuapem Twi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akuapem Twi is a dialect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> language spoken on the Akuapem ridge in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. In the 19th century Basel missionaries, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottlieb-christaller">Johann Gottlieb Christaller</a>, chose it as the basis of written Twi, publishing a grammar, a dictionary and a complete Bible translation, finished in 1871. It long served as the standard literary form of Akan.</p></div>
